# server/ is NO LONGER excluded — api/index.js require()s it, so the
# Express app now ships as a Vercel serverless function. Excluding it
# would build a frontend whose every /api call 404s.

# The container deployment plane. It is a Docker stack that runs on its own
# VM — compose file, worker, Postgres schema — and nothing under server/ or
# api/ require()s it. On Vercel it is 4MB of source that can never execute,
# and its own package.json sitting in the tree only gives the build another
# manifest to get confused by.
deploy/

# Dev/build scratch
scratch/
*.py

# Local tooling
.claude/
node_modules/

# Tests and docs never need to reach a deployment
server/tests/
docs/

# The scaffold is NOT excluded. It used to be, to silence spurious TS2307
# warnings in the build log — but the root tsconfig.json already excludes
# "server/lib/codeagent/scaffold/**/*", which solves that properly, and
# excluding the files here solved it by deleting them from the deployment.
#
# scaffold-files.js reads this directory at request time to assemble a
# project's source before uploading it to the deploy plane. With src/ and
# vite.config.ts missing, every deployed app shipped a tree whose
# index.html pointed at a /src/main.tsx that was not there, and the build
# died with "Rollup failed to resolve import /src/main.tsx".

# Test and demo scripts — not imported by the app, just inflate the bundle.
server/*-test.js
server/*-demo.js
server/dev-admin-verify.js
